play with the fast check; the one with the fewest failing states (then the largest step-free run)\n   is kept and fully checked at every state;\n - each approach starts from the re-targeted play state that is nearest (in the source) to its first state;\n - every kept state gets the full planning check (Checker.check full: 10 mm robot-environment, 5 mm gripper/held-\n   environment, ranges; in a food approach the r19prepchain contact window, never touching).\nSo the held object, the gripper and the cart follow EXACTLY the certified UR5e path; only the arm links differ.\nAccepted per state: TCP within POSE_MM (0.5 mm) and 0.2 deg of the source, joint step <= 10 deg, no hits. A pass is\nan ordinary chain json and must still pass r19prep_verify.py (<= 4 mm). A failure is reported state by state:\nthe failing pair, its exact clearance (distance.py lower bound) against the gate, and where (between which keyframes).\npython r19fr5prep_retarget.py SRC=<UR5e chain json> ARM=fr5_j6_pgc_sp20 [NSTART=8] [TAG=rt]\n -> results/r19/fr5/prep/chain_<act>_<TAG>_<arm>.json", "source": "results/r19/prep/chain_tubfill_t15fin_ur5e_enc2_pgc.json", "source_arm": "ur5e_enc2_pgc", "argv": ["ACT=tubfill", "SEEDS=1", "TRIES=10", "KEEP=3", "TPITCH=15", "ARM=ur5e_enc2_pgc_m2"], "scene_used": "src", "current_code_same": {"scene": false, "grasp_worlds": false, "keyframes": true}, "bad_runs_play": [], "bad_runs_approach": [], "start_screen": [{"start": "mapped source state", "bad_states": 0, "first_bad": null, "max_step_deg": 4.69}, {"start": "solver start 0 (3.0 mm)", "bad_states": 77, "first_bad": 25, "max_step_deg": 3.1}, {"start": "solver start 1 (3.0 mm)", "bad_states": 0, "first_bad": null, "max_step_deg": 3.02}, {"start": "solver start 2 (3.0 mm)", "bad_states": 77, "first_bad": 25, "max_step_deg": 3.1}, {"start": "solver start 3 (3.0 mm)", "bad_states": 0, "first_bad": null, "max_step_deg": 3.02}, {"start": "solver start 4 (3.0 mm)", "bad_states": 77, "first_bad": 25, "max_step_deg": 3.1}, 